  text-size: 2.4vmin
</slide>

## Slides, sections, blocks and clicks

A **slide** is one `.slide` file. In it you write text (Markdown), images, charts and **code blocks** in reading order.
A `<code>` is one animated block, and its `<frame>`s are the states it passes through, one click each:

<code lang=text>
  <code lang=ts>
    <frame>let a = 1;</frame>         <- block "fn", state 1
    <frame>let a = 2;</frame>         <- state 2: the tokens morph 1 -> 2
  \</code>
  <code lang=py>print("independent")\</code>   <- another block, no relation

  <section> ... \</section>         <- a slide can swap whole sections under a shared <head>
</code>

Blocks with the **same `id`** are one animation, in the same place, even across sections and slides:
that is how code keeps morphing while the text around it changes.

<notes>
  The most important idea of the tool. Take your time here.
</notes>
